\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Experimental workflow. Twenty puzzles per stratum are paired with solver configurations (seven SAT, one CP-SAT, one backtracking). Each run executes under a 10.0-second wall-clock timeout and a 60\% available-memory resource guard; pairwise and binary SAT encodings at \(N=81\) are predeclared excluded by the guard. Every returned solution is independently verified by \texttt  {is\textunderscore \penalty 0\hspace  {0pt}valid\textunderscore \penalty 0\hspace  {0pt}solution\textunderscore \penalty 0\hspace  {0pt}for\textunderscore \penalty 0\hspace  {0pt}puzzle} before a run is classified as \texttt  {SOLVED\textunderscore \penalty 0\hspace  {0pt}VALID}. Result statuses feed the aggregate, per-configuration, and stratified analyses in Section~\ref {sec:results}. Excluded runs are not attempted and therefore do not enter the run or validation stages.}}{13}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:workflow}{{1}{13}{Experimental workflow. Twenty puzzles per stratum are paired with solver configurations (seven SAT, one CP-SAT, one backtracking). Each run executes under a 10.0-second wall-clock timeout and a 60\% available-memory resource guard; pairwise and binary SAT encodings at \(N=81\) are predeclared excluded by the guard. Every returned solution is independently verified by \texttt {is\_valid\_solution\_for\_puzzle} before a run is classified as \texttt {SOLVED\_VALID}. Result statuses feed the aggregate, per-configuration, and stratified analyses in Section~\ref {sec:results}. Excluded runs are not attempted and therefore do not enter the run or validation stages}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overall solver-family comparison. Panel (a): valid-solution rate (valid solutions / attempted runs). Panel (b): timeout rate (timeouts / attempted runs). SAT pools seven configurations across 760 attempted runs; CP-SAT and backtracking are single configurations across 120 attempted runs each. SAT's denominator excludes 80 predeclared memory-guard exclusions (pairwise and binary at \(N=81\)). All rates are descriptive single measurements with no significance testing.}}{14}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overall}{{2}{14}{Overall solver-family comparison. Panel (a): valid-solution rate (valid solutions / attempted runs). Panel (b): timeout rate (timeouts / attempted runs). SAT pools seven configurations across 760 attempted runs; CP-SAT and backtracking are single configurations across 120 attempted runs each. SAT's denominator excludes 80 predeclared memory-guard exclusions (pairwise and binary at \(N=81\)). All rates are descriptive single measurements with no significance testing}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Per-SAT-configuration comparison. Panel (a): valid-solution rate of attempted runs. Panel (b): timeout rate of attempted runs. Pairwise and binary each show inflated rates on attempted runs because 40 of their \(N=81\) instances are predeclared excluded by the memory guard (attempted = 80 rather than 120); over all 120 recorded cells their rates would be approximately 51.67\% and 50.00\%. Commander has one live resource-guard rejection. The spread among configurations is small (50.00\%--77.50\% valid on attempted runs) and no significance test is performed.}}{14}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:satconfigs}{{3}{14}{Per-SAT-configuration comparison. Panel (a): valid-solution rate of attempted runs. Panel (b): timeout rate of attempted runs. Pairwise and binary each show inflated rates on attempted runs because 40 of their \(N=81\) instances are predeclared excluded by the memory guard (attempted = 80 rather than 120); over all 120 recorded cells their rates would be approximately 51.67\% and 50.00\%. Commander has one live resource-guard rejection. The spread among configurations is small (50.00\%--77.50\% valid on attempted runs) and no significance test is performed}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Stratified performance by grid size \(N\) and removal ratio \(r\). Valid-solution rate per solver family across the six strata (20 instances per stratum). SAT pools seven configurations; its attempted count per stratum is 140 at \(N=9\) and \(N=36\), and 100 at \(N=81\) after removing 40 predeclared memory-guard exclusions (pairwise and binary). CP-SAT and backtracking attempt 20 runs per stratum. Zero-height bars denote 0\% valid rate; excluded runs are not drawn as bars but are noted in the caption. SAT's valid rate at \(N=81\) is 0\% (0 valid / 100 attempted); CP-SAT and backtracking also reach 0\% at \(N=81\). The \(N=36, r=0.5\) stratum is the hardest for all families (below 21\%).}}{15}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stratified}{{4}{15}{Stratified performance by grid size \(N\) and removal ratio \(r\). Valid-solution rate per solver family across the six strata (20 instances per stratum). SAT pools seven configurations; its attempted count per stratum is 140 at \(N=9\) and \(N=36\), and 100 at \(N=81\) after removing 40 predeclared memory-guard exclusions (pairwise and binary). CP-SAT and backtracking attempt 20 runs per stratum. Zero-height bars denote 0\% valid rate; excluded runs are not drawn as bars but are noted in the caption. SAT's valid rate at \(N=81\) is 0\% (0 valid / 100 attempted); CP-SAT and backtracking also reach 0\% at \(N=81\). The \(N=36, r=0.5\) stratum is the hardest for all families (below 21\%)}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Encoding complexity versus observed outcome (descriptive; no correlation claimed). Panel (a): total CNF clauses versus grid size \(N\) for each AMO encoding, computed exactly from the formulas in \texttt  {src/sudoku/solvers/sat.py} (one ALO clause plus AMO clauses per exactly-one group, plus clue-unit clauses). Pairwise and binary at \(N=81\) exceed the 60\% available-RAM memory guard and were predeclared excluded (no data point plotted). Panel (b): observed outcome counts per stratum for SAT (pooled seven configurations), showing valid, timeout, predeclared-excluded, and live-guard-rejection runs. Runtimes are successful-run-only and timeout-censored; no statistical correlation between clause count and runtime has been analyzed. Pairwise/binary at \(N=81\) are excluded rather than timed out, so their runtime performance at that size remains unknown.}}{16}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:complexity}{{5}{16}{Encoding complexity versus observed outcome (descriptive; no correlation claimed). Panel (a): total CNF clauses versus grid size \(N\) for each AMO encoding, computed exactly from the formulas in \texttt {src/sudoku/solvers/sat.py} (one ALO clause plus AMO clauses per exactly-one group, plus clue-unit clauses). Pairwise and binary at \(N=81\) exceed the 60\% available-RAM memory guard and were predeclared excluded (no data point plotted). Panel (b): observed outcome counts per stratum for SAT (pooled seven configurations), showing valid, timeout, predeclared-excluded, and live-guard-rejection runs. Runtimes are successful-run-only and timeout-censored; no statistical correlation between clause count and runtime has been analyzed. Pairwise/binary at \(N=81\) are excluded rather than timed out, so their runtime performance at that size remains unknown}{figure.5}{}}
